WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:04.670
It's a miracle that Jaya Sable is still alive.

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:10.120
She was disfigured by an acid attack, and
she has suffered from its effects for years.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:15.090
Her brother Satish has taken his 27-year-old
sister to get her twelfth operation.

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:18.670
Jaya's attacker was her husband and his parents.

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:25.250
The reason: she had given birth to a baby
girl instead of a boy.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:30.150
"Nobody from my husband’s family came to
visit me in the hospital -- because I gave

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.410
birth to a girl."

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:37.649
Dr. Ganesh Rakh specializes in cases like
Jaya's.

00:00:37.649 --> 00:00:40.290
He helps her feel human again.

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:47.899
For years, he's been campaigning against women
aborting their female fetuses or killing their

00:00:47.899 --> 00:00:51.850
baby girls.

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:56.480
He's become something of a hero for taking
no payment whenever a girl is delivered in

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.160
his clinic.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.579
"The thinking here is that the family isn’t
complete without a boy.

00:01:03.579 --> 00:01:06.869
Males are seen as the ones who carry on the
family’s lineage.

00:01:06.869 --> 00:01:08.479
Girls are seen as a burden.

00:01:08.479 --> 00:01:11.729
The girl’s family has to pay a large dowry
to see her married.

00:01:11.729 --> 00:01:16.459
They also have to pay all the wedding expenses."

00:01:16.459 --> 00:01:21.630
Using ultrasound to determine the sex of a
fetus is strictly prohibited in India.

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:24.819
But it's still widespread, Dr. Rakh says.

00:01:24.819 --> 00:01:26.659
It's just a question of money.

00:01:26.659 --> 00:01:31.450
Angel, who's just six days old, is in many
ways lucky to be alive.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:36.380
Her parents didn't know her gender until she
was born.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.779
Her grandmother had hoped for a boy.

00:01:38.779 --> 00:01:44.340
As a mother of six girls, she suffered under
social pressure until the birth of her seventh

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:50.679
child, a boy.

00:01:50.679 --> 00:01:52.679
"I felt like I was finally successful.

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:56.299
At last, everyone one shut their mouths.

00:01:56.299 --> 00:02:00.229
People had made it a point to come and visit
me when I had daughters so they could taunt

00:02:00.229 --> 00:02:01.229
me.

00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:02.939
They stopped after I had my son."

00:02:02.939 --> 00:02:09.030
Dr. Rakh continues his outreach wherever he
can.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:14.040
Away from his clinic, he offers encouragement
to pregnant women who are wary of giving birth

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.760
to baby girls.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:20.319
"Sometimes we need to pay more attention to
a case.

00:02:20.319 --> 00:02:26.010
If I feel that a patient has reacted negatively
when I tell her she might have a girl, then

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:28.879
she should have more counseling and follow
up.

00:02:28.879 --> 00:02:36.700
Our aim is to ensure that the fetus remains
healthy and grows well, and won't be aborted.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:41.140
On this evening, Angel and her mother are
sent home from the clinic with flowers and

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:42.140
cake.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:44.900
Usually this kind of celebration with cake
and flowers is reserved for women who've just

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:45.969
delivered baby boys.

00:02:45.969 --> 00:02:49.579
But on this evening, there's a different rallying
call.

00:02:49.579 --> 00:02:53.879
These people are chanting, "Save the girlchild,
save the country.”

